# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Drives GitHub's "Cite this repository" button. Zenodo takes its record metadata from
# .zenodo.json, which carries the same author and licence — keep the two in step.
#
# No version or release date here on purpose: a citation minted per release takes the
# version from the tag, and a field that has to be remembered is a field that goes stale.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: decern
message: If you refer to decern, please cite it as below.
type: software
abstract: >-
  An authorization kernel whose decision function carries nine invariants discharged over the
  whole input space by an SMT solver, and a tamper-evident ledger that records each decision so
  a third party can verify what was decided and that the record was not altered afterwards.
authors:
  - family-names: Aravind
    given-names: Anivar A
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-8995-0005
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21848620
repository-code: https://github.com/anivar/decern
url: https://decern.anivar.net/
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - authorization
  - policy decision point
  - formal verification
  - SMT
  - transparency log
  - accountability
  - AI agents
